## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public `frontend-next/`
  beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- D1 Account Seller Overview, D2 Region Canonical Data Foundation, D2 Region Sell
  + Explore + Search + AI, D3-A requested-price context/history and D5 Auth Entry
  Flow are closed on `origin/main`. The D3-B branch baseline and merge-base is
  `58275d8f08c5b5af6eb8d8e715ac674be3091c9d`.
- D3-B adds cellar acquisition facts, forward-only D3-A reference snapshots and
  an owner-only `cellar_portfolio_analitica()` RPC. Browser analytics use exactly
  that RPC: no analytics table reads, query per bottle, query per graph point or
  external provider call was introduced.
- Accounting preserves `NULL` as unknown and zero as known zero. Vinea purchases
  use authoritative paid net outflow after refunds and override manual cost;
  realized seller income requires transferred payout state, transfer timestamp
  and amount. Net performance is current known D3-A reference value plus realized
  transferred income minus known acquisition outflow; incomplete facts reduce
  coverage instead of becoming zero.
- D3-A reference semantics remain same wine, same format, active asking prices,
  at least three comparables and median price. No `prezzoMercato`, linked-listing,
  completed-sale or payment-price fallback was added.
- Snapshot history is append-only and forward-only. A real snapshot with a null
  median interrupts coverage from that instant; no prior median is carried
  forward and no historical value is invented before the first observation.
  Opening `/cantina` does not write snapshots.
- `Wine` remains the catalog/presentation model and
  `PosizionePortafoglioRow` remains the accounting read model. `/cantina` shows
  D3-B reference value, known capital, transferred income, net performance and
  an accessible value-over-time chart/table. Analytics failure is fail-soft and
  leaves ordinary cellar data, layout, 3D view and drinking-window information
  available. Database permission, timeout, unknown and arbitrary `P0001` errors
  are mediated and do not reach the UI.
- Migration `20260826130000_d3b_cellar_accounting.sql` follows the frozen D2
  migration `20260826120000_wine_regions_canonical.sql`. A fresh disposable
  PostgreSQL 17 replay after the rename applied 40 migrations plus the genuine
  pre-migration fixture and produced **39 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**, with every
  fixture and generated observation removed and every residue counter at zero.
- Bun 1.3.14 validation is green: frozen install unchanged; targeted D3-B tests
  **46 pass / 0 fail**; full `frontend-next` suite **1035 pass / 0 fail / 18,528
  expect() calls across 63 files**; typecheck and build pass. Lint has zero errors
  and 13 unrelated existing warnings. CI `MIN_TESTS` is raised from 989 to the
  measured passing count, 1035. `git diff --check` is clean.
- No production order, bottle or other fixture was created. No production write,
  provider activation, manual migration application, commit, push, PR or merge
